    "body": "This could be achieved through checking to see if `$MSYSTEM` or `$CYGWIN` are set. Once either one is set, either the `cygpath` executable could be called (although this doesn't solve `/c/msys64` displaying properly as it will always resolve it to `/`. Alternatively calling `pwd` (which should be available on all Unix-like environments) or probing the `$PWD` environment variable could work, though I'm not sure all shells properly set that",
